speechtext:
The question my hon.
friend raised regarding the British war medal I submitted to my department this morning, but I have not been able to get the information so far. X will submit it to him privately ;
I could not obtain it before coming here. The question of medals for those who served in Canada is one that has been before the department, as my hon. friend knows, for years, and it has always struck me that it would be a good thing if the men who served only in Canada could be given some distinctive medal. But the cost is pretty heavy, and up to the present time no minister has seen fit to recommend that the expenditure be made just yet. If I remember rightly, the cost would be about $1,000,000 or a little more, and owing to the financial condition of the country we have thought it best to postpone the matter for a while. That is a plain statement of the situation.
